The best example I can think of, that helps me understand {zi'o}, is to=20
realize that {cliva} is {klama be zi'o} (really {klama be zi'o bei fu=20
zi'o}, but it's the lack of destination that makes the difference.)=C2=A0=
=20
Similarly, {litru} is {klama be zi'o bei zi'o}.=C2=A0 Not that you can't ha=
ve=20
a source or a destination when you {litru}, but they are not only=20
irrelevant, there are not any part of the assertion.

(can {zo'e} not ever wind up meaning {no da}?=C2=A0 It makes sense that it=
=20
shouldn't, but was there a counterexample to that...?)

~mark

